.TH SDE-UPDATE 1 "October 2026" "SDE" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sde-update \- preview and install system updates on DebION GNU/Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sde-update
[--check | --version | --plan ACTION | --transaction ACTION]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Shows source-grouped updates from the local APT cache. The read-only Python APT
model is adapted from Mint Update with its original GPLv3+ copyright preserved.
Held packages are excluded. The frontend does not add repositories or start an
automatic background updater.
.PP
Refresh Sources opens a terminal for PackageKit's cache refresh. Install Updates
opens PackageKit's interactive update transaction. Review the final package list
and confirm there. The system's polkit policy controls authorization. Press
Enter in the terminal afterward to reload the native preview.
.PP
Debian testing transitions can require manual APT decisions; a preview from the
local cache does not guarantee that every upgrade is currently resolvable.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --check
Print the versioned tab-separated read-only update metadata and exit.
.TP
.B --plan refresh|upgrade
Print the fixed PackageKit argument vector without running it.
.TP
.B --transaction refresh|upgrade
Run the fixed interactive PackageKit operation in the current terminal.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pkgcli (1),
.BR pkcon (1),
.BR sde-suite (1),
.BR apt (8)
